Version 1.1
- BUG: Current language now correctly preselected in preferences dialog
- BUG: Length of a note cannot be scaled down to less than 1 tick any more
- ENH: Use 64 bits precision when changing MIDI file resolution
- ENH: Minor changes in view layout and colors

Version 1.0
- CHG: One single Qt project for PortMidi and SpeedyMidi
- CHG: new source code directory structure
- CHG: updated INSTALL instructions
- CHG: updated PortMidi to version 1.27
- NEW: Extended PortMidi to support an immediate callback on input on all OSes
- NEW: MidiThru
- CHG: Installer introduction texts (English/German)
- BUG: crash when trying to show a message box during dropEvent
- NEW: Tool tips
- ENH: Simpler pasting
- BUG: fixed MousePiano key event routing problem
- ENH: ESC turns all notes off on mouse piano
- ENH: Now also loads RIFF/RMID files
- BUG: Now correctly loads format 1 MIDI files with a conductor track integrated into first real track
- ENH: Vertical scroll bar now supports correct page stepping
- CHG: Renamed menu "MIDI" to "Playback"
- CHG: Moved menu commands modifying "Record" flag to menu "Write"
- BUG: Swing algorithm now works correctly with tied notes of all lengths
- BUG: Main window layout sometimes corrupted when opening a file from explorer
- BUG: Saving failed when current program working directory was not writable
- CHG: Playback now starts from cursor position by default
- ENH: Position and click-rects of S/M/R flags on track header
- CHG: prepared projects and Code for compilation on Mac
- BUG: Crash in PortMidi/PortTime component for Mac
- NEW: Patch assignment in track wizard as an option
- ENH: Upper bound for track height in sequencer view
- General code cleanup, typos in code corrected

